    {
      "round": 2,
      "decision": "revise",
      "checked_flows": [
        "Layout after revision: top bar / tab row / board / Licenses vertical positions now line up with the observed app",
        "Custom Game dialog: grid slider 9x9, mines slider 20 -> '(24%)' confirming truncated percentage",
        "Custom 9x9 / 20-mine board: first tap flood-reveals with 1 blue, 2 green, 3 red and 4 purple digits",
        "Custom 9x9 / 2-mine board: first tap cascades to a win with green banner, sunglasses face, mines auto-flagged, counter 000",
        "Easy preset board: long-press on a covered tile places a flag and decrements the counter 010 -> 009",
        "Covered tile styling after revision: darker slate gradient with a tighter corner radius",
        "Tab glyphs after revision: Easy bomb with fuse, Custom gear"
      ],
      "findings": [
        "Defect: after the first tap on a freshly created custom board (reproduced on 5x5/2-mine and 9x9/20-mine), the board stops accepting touches - further taps on covered tiles and long presses both do nothing while the tab row, face button and dialogs stay responsive. The Easy preset accepted a tap followed by a long press, so the per-cell pointerInput nodes are the suspect.",
        "Planned fix: replace the 25-289 per-cell pointerInput handlers with one board-level pointerInput that maps the touch offset to a row/column, which also removes any dependence on cell size.",
        "Also confirmed in this round: mine percentage is now truncated (20 of 81 shows 24%, not 25%)."
      ],
