    {
      "round": 3,
      "decision": "accept",
      "checked_flows": [
        "Easy board: four consecutive board gestures (two taps, a long-press flag and another tap) all register after the gesture-handling rewrite",
        "Long-press flag toggles the orange flag and decreases the mine counter 010 -> 009, remaining flags stay consistent after a loss (10 mines, 3 flags -> 007)",
        "Chording: tapping a revealed '2' with two adjacent flags reveals the remaining covered neighbour; when a flag was wrong the uncovered mine explodes with a starburst and the round ends with 'Game Over', X-eyed face and every mine revealed",
        "Custom Game dialog: grid slider 5x5, mines slider 3 -> '3 (12%)', fog and safe-first-tap switches, Cancel/Start",
        "Custom 5x5 / 3-mine board: first tap cascades, then a long-press flag and a further tap both work (previously the board stopped responding)",
        "Custom 5x5 / 16-mine board: first tap wins the round, all mines auto-flagged, counter 000, green 'You Win!' banner, sunglasses face",
        "Hard tab: 16x17 board, counter 050, amber 03:00 countdown; digits fade to violet tiles about 20s after reveal while empty cells stay dark",
        "Restart: app relaunches into a fresh Easy game (counter 010, 00:00, Easy tab) - no persistence, matching the observed app",
        "Licenses dialog opens from the bottom label with monospace scrollable notice and a pinned teal Close button"
      ],
      "findings": [
        "Board gestures now use one board-level pointerInput that maps the touch offset to a row/column, so a freshly created board keeps accepting taps and long presses - the earlier 'board stops responding after the first tap' defect is fixed.",
        "Digit fade timing is wall-clock based, so on the slow emulator the violet fade can appear a few seconds after the 20s mark; behaviour itself matches the observed app (only digit cells fade, empty cells stay dark).",
        "No private or session data exists in the project or APK: the app declares no permissions, has no network use and its only text content is the licence notice."
      ],
